From: Juan Carlos Garcia <jgarcia@cloudlinux.com>
Date: Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Complete the CVE-2025-1736 backport (upstream bug #79265)

Follow-up to php-7.0-CVE-2025-1736.patch, which is already applied in this
package.  That patch tightened the header-boundary test to require a full
CRLF, but kept PHP 7.0's open-coded single strstr() at each call site.

Backport of the following upstream commits:

    --- 01 ---
    From d0d60503b54b528d42546acf1ca34914fb8aea55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
    From: Miguel Xavier Penha Neto <miguelxpn2@gmail.com>
    Date: Mon, 24 Feb 2020 02:04:37 -0300
    Subject: [PATCH] Fixes #79265: Improper injection of Host header when using
     fopen for http requests

    Check all occurrences of the string "host:" (and other headers),
    not just the first one.

    --- 02 ---
    From cc704f5bb6bfbb7b17595f7ff24af011d66374a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
    From: Nikita Popov <nikita.ppv@gmail.com>
    Date: Mon, 24 Feb 2020 09:58:29 +0100
    Subject: [PATCH] Reduce code duplication in HTTP header checks

    --- 03 ---
    From 56cdbe63c24b86c2f1d60bf2609fde113d12d235 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
    From: Nikita Popov <nikita.ppv@gmail.com>
    Date: Mon, 24 Feb 2020 10:19:58 +0100
    Subject: [PATCH] Don't treat any WS as start of header

    Check that the header occurs after \n, not other whitespace
    characters.

Why this is needed.

The CVE fix (upstream 963551715a) is a one-line change INSIDE upstream's
check_has_header() helper.  That helper LOOPS over every occurrence of the
header name, and it was made to do so by commit 01 in February 2020 - five
years before the CVE fix was written against it.  PHP 7.0 has no such helper:
the test is open-coded at eight call sites, each doing a single strstr().

Tightening the predicate without the loop makes the post-patch detection set
a strict subset of the pre-patch one.  A decoy occurrence of the header name
earlier in the blob now defeats detection, and PHP emits a DUPLICATE Host,
Content-Length or Authorization where both stock 7.0.33 and upstream emit
one.  That is upstream bug #79265 exactly, which commit 01 exists to fix.

Demonstrated on php-7.0.33 built three ways from a single tree (--disable-all
--enable-pcntl --enable-posix), captured off the wire by a local listener,
for the blob "X-Note: about host:foo\r\nHost: real.example\r\n":

    stock 7.0.33                 Host: real.example                (one)
    with CVE-2025-1736 patch     Host: 127.0.0.1:NNNN              (TWO)
                                 Host: real.example
    with this patch on top       Host: real.example                (one)

Adaptation notes:

  * check_has_header() is introduced verbatim from upstream except for the
    added (s - headers >= 2) bound: unlike upstream we must not read *(s-2)
    when the match starts at the second byte of the blob.  Upstream carries
    that one-byte-left exposure in the helper itself; reported separately.
    It is placed just above strip_header() rather than just below it, so the
    hunk anchors on the HTTP_WRAPPER_* defines and applies at fuzz 0 both
    against a pristine tarball and in series.

  * All seven have_header sites are converted.  The site under
    "/* remove Proxy-Authorization header */" is left byte-identical to
    7.0.33, as php-7.0-CVE-2025-1736.patch already left it.  It gates a
    REMOVAL - PHP strips the caller's Proxy-Authorization before tunnelling
    through CONNECT - so a predicate that wrongly returns false is fail-open
    and replays the proxy credential to the origin.  Upstream narrows that
    site to (s == t || *(s-1) == '\n'); we deliberately do not.

  * Upstream's own bug79265.phpt and bug79265_2.phpt are carried (they ship in
    php-7.3.33 and later). They already use server.inc, so they need no
    rewrite. They are the pair that separates this change from what is in
    master: with the predicate tightened but no loop, bug79265_2 passes while
    bug79265 FAILS - one half of #79265 traded for the other.

  * The three upstream GHSA tests are also carried, rewritten for this
    branch's harness. PHP 7.0's ServerClientTestCase has no message-passing
    phpt_notify() and no {{ ADDR }} substitution, so they use
    ext/standard/tests/http/server.inc and its $output request capture - the
    idiom of the neighbouring bug61548.phpt. Expected output is HTTP/1.0,
    this branch's default protocol_version.

Test results on php-7.0.33, one tree built three ways, run-tests.php over the
five tests:

    build                          failing tests
    stock 7.0.33                   bug79265, bug79265_2, ghsa-...-001
    master today (CVE patch only)  bug79265
    master + this patch            none

The same correction is being made on the open changes for alt-php71
(CL 270674) and alt-php55 (CL 270692).  alt-php73 and later are unaffected:
they ship >= 7.3.33, which already carries the looping helper.
---
diff -Naur a/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c b/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c
--- a/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c	2026-09-03 12:46:16.940740437 +0200
+++ b/ext/standard/http_fopen_wrapper.c	2026-09-03 12:46:16.945897758 +0200
@@ -85,6 +85,17 @@
 #define HTTP_WRAPPER_HEADER_INIT    1
 #define HTTP_WRAPPER_REDIRECTED     2
 
+static zend_bool check_has_header(const char *headers, const char *header) {
+	const char *s = headers;
+	while ((s = strstr(s, header))) {
+		if (s == headers || (s - headers >= 2 && *(s-1) == '\n' && *(s-2) == '\r')) {
+			return 1;
+		}
+		s++;
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static inline void strip_header(char *header_bag, char *lc_header_bag,
 		const char *lc_header_name)
 {
@@ -471,33 +482,26 @@
 				strip_header(user_headers, t, "content-type:");
 			}
 
-			if ((s = strstr(t, "user-agent:")) &&
-			    (s == t || (s - t >= 2 && *(s-1) == '\n' && *(s-2) == '\r'))) {
-				 have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_USER_AGENT;
-			}
-			if ((s = strstr(t, "host:")) &&
-			    (s == t || (s - t >= 2 && *(s-1) == '\n' && *(s-2) == '\r'))) {
-				 have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_HOST;
-			}
-			if ((s = strstr(t, "from:")) &&
-			    (s == t || (s - t >= 2 && *(s-1) == '\n' && *(s-2) == '\r'))) {
-				 have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_FROM;
-				}
-			if ((s = strstr(t, "authorization:")) &&
-			    (s == t || (s - t >= 2 && *(s-1) == '\n' && *(s-2) == '\r'))) {
-				 have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_AUTH;
-			}
-			if ((s = strstr(t, "content-length:")) &&
-			    (s == t || (s - t >= 2 && *(s-1) == '\n' && *(s-2) == '\r'))) {
-				 have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_CONTENT_LENGTH;
-			}
-			if ((s = strstr(t, "content-type:")) &&
-			    (s == t || (s - t >= 2 && *(s-1) == '\n' && *(s-2) == '\r'))) {
-				 have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_TYPE;
-			}
-			if ((s = strstr(t, "connection:")) &&
-			    (s == t || (s - t >= 2 && *(s-1) == '\n' && *(s-2) == '\r'))) {
-				 have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_CONNECTION;
+			if (check_has_header(t, "user-agent:")) {
+				have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_USER_AGENT;
+			}
+			if (check_has_header(t, "host:")) {
+				have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_HOST;
+			}
+			if (check_has_header(t, "from:")) {
+				have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_FROM;
+			}
+			if (check_has_header(t, "authorization:")) {
+				have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_AUTH;
+			}
+			if (check_has_header(t, "content-length:")) {
+				have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_CONTENT_LENGTH;
+			}
+			if (check_has_header(t, "content-type:")) {
+				have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_TYPE;
+			}
+			if (check_has_header(t, "connection:")) {
+				have_header |= HTTP_HEADER_CONNECTION;
 			}
 			/* remove Proxy-Authorization header */
 			if (use_proxy && use_ssl && (s = strstr(t, "proxy-authorization:")) &&
diff -Naur a/ext/standard/tests/http/bug79265_2.phpt b/ext/standard/tests/http/bug79265_2.phpt
--- a/ext/standard/tests/http/bug79265_2.phpt	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/ext/standard/tests/http/bug79265_2.phpt	2026-09-03 12:46:16.950630266 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+--TEST--
+Bug #79265 variation: "host:" not at start of header
+--INI--
+allow_url_fopen=1
+--SKIPIF--
+<?php require 'server.inc'; http_server_skipif('tcp://127.0.0.1:12342'); ?>
+--FILE--
+<?php
+require 'server.inc';
+
+$responses = array(
+    "data://text/plain,HTTP/1.0 200 OK\r\n\r\n",
+);
+
+$pid = http_server("tcp://127.0.0.1:12342", $responses, $output);
+
+$opts = array(
+  'http'=>array(
+    'method'=>"GET",
+    'header'=>"RandomHeader: host:8080\r\n" .
+              "Cookie: foo=bar\r\n"
+  )
+);
+$context = stream_context_create($opts);
+$fd = fopen('http://127.0.0.1:12342/', 'rb', false, $context);
+fseek($output, 0, SEEK_SET);
+echo stream_get_contents($output);
+fclose($fd);
+
+http_server_kill($pid);
+
+?>
+--EXPECT--
+GET / HTTP/1.0
+Host: 127.0.0.1:12342
+Connection: close
+RandomHeader: host:8080
+Cookie: foo=bar
